        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For most damp basements, DRYLOK Extreme brushed onto clean, bare masonry is the safest single purchase: it has a published pressure rating, it fills block pores, and it is sold everywhere. If your walls are unpainted poured concrete and you want them to look unchanged, a penetrating sealer such as RadonSeal Plus is the better fit.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Whichever you choose, the order of work matters more than the brand. Move roof water away from the house, scrub off the salts, patch the cracks, then coat. A sealer applied in that sequence earns its price; one applied over efflorescence next to a dumping downspout rarely lasts a winter.
          </p>
